 ## Overview
-Voxel Chunk Meshing with Culling is a surface extraction method that generates a triangle mesh from a 3D voxel grid by emitting geometry only for voxel faces adjacent to empty space, thereby eliminating hidden internal faces [G]. Builds on [Marching Cubes](774-marching-cubes.md). It differs from [Naive Voxel Meshing](2376-naive-voxel-meshing.md) by actively checking neighbor states to suppress redundant geometry, and from [Face Culling Voxel Meshing](2268-face-culling-voxel-meshing.md) by serving as the foundational algorithmic family from which specific culling implementations are derived.
